
Automated Passwordless SCP Setup Instructions
--------------------------------------------

1. Install OpenSSH Client on Windows (if not already installed).

2. Generate an SSH key on Windows:
   ssh-keygen -t rsa -b 4096
   - Save at default location
   - No passphrase (press Enter twice)

3. Copy the public key to the Linux host:
   scp C:\Users\USERNAME\.ssh\id_rsa.pub root@linuxbox:/root/

4. Install the key on the Linux machine:
   sudo mkdir -p /root/.ssh
   sudo cat /root/id_rsa.pub >> /root/.ssh/authorized_keys
   sudo chmod 600 /root/.ssh/authorized_keys
   sudo chmod 700 /root/.ssh
   sudo rm /root/id_rsa.pub

5. Test passwordless login from Windows:
   ssh root@linuxbox
   - Should log in with no password

6. Automate SCP in your Windows token service:
   scp C:\TokenService\current_token.txt root@linuxbox:/root/current_token

7. Recommended: Secure the Linux file so only root can read it:
   sudo chmod 600 /root/current_token

8. Optional: Restrict root SSH access only from Windows IP by modifying authorized_keys:
   from="WINDOWS_IP_ADDRESS" ssh-rsa AAAA...

This provides fully automated, secure, passwordless token transfer from Windows to Linux, storing the token only where root can access it.
